    "reason": "[ev-853844eb542e] says that setting the `ValidateCAA` feature gate is now a no-op that only prints a warning log line. It does not limit this to setting the gate to true. So any environment that sets the gate explicitly, enabled or disabled, is exposed, and any[feature-gate enabled, feature-gate disabled] expresses exactly that. P3's enabled-only condition is narrower because it misses environments that set the gate to false, which also get the setting ignored and the warning.",
